    "done_when": "Done when a new tests/test_a_session_host_never_blocks_in_its_read.py shows four cases. (a) Two readers share one FIFO, and the other reader takes the bytes after select reports them; the host under test returns from that pass and runs tick within two poll intervals. (b) A stop request with a wake-pipe write ends a host in that state within two poll intervals. (c) A second host started for an owner pair whose lock is held exits with a stated reason and leaves the FIFO in place. (d) A host whose FIFO path now names a different FIFO does not unlink it at stop. The negative control restores the blocking read, which makes (a) and (b) exceed a per-test timeout, and drops the inode check, which makes (d) unlink. The test files importing reckon.crew.session_host add no failure against the base revision, run one arm at a time with at most -n 4 . Ruff check and ruff format --check add no findings on the staged paths. Write paths: reckon/crew/session_host.py and the new test.",
